From 924781e68d157b86601ac293bd46f3672a7ec362 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 21:01:26 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 03/28] WIP: the F32/tiny-M kernels, the default flips, and the
 W=1..8 width-purity probe

Squashed theme commit (5 originals): F32 dense weights off by default + the
always-QSA prefill flip (drops the dense shortcut); the shape-aware F32 dense
split (MMB for the MoE router only); the warp-per-token tiny-M F32 kernel for
the hc *_inject GEMMs; its MMAX=4 specialisation + TT sweep; and the W=1..8
logits width-purity probe (a tools/ harness, the last promotion gate).
